WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.820 --> 00:00:03.440
Horror movies have to really stick the landing
to last.

00:00:03.500 --> 00:00:08.280
Whether that means coming in with a surprise
twist, or an explosive event, or even a maddening

00:00:08.290 --> 00:00:11.940
cliffhanger, the final moments of any good
thriller should bring together all the jump

00:00:11.940 --> 00:00:15.000
scares and eerie elements that have defined
the rest of the movie.

00:00:15.240 --> 00:00:19.570
For these modern flicks, the third acts were
so good that they'll easily stand the test

00:00:19.570 --> 00:00:20.120
of time.

00:00:20.260 --> 00:00:23.700
Let's take a look at the best horror movie
endings of the century so far.

00:00:23.700 --> 00:00:26.440
And don't be scared, but there are huge spoilers
ahead.

00:00:26.880 --> 00:00:27.540
The Others

00:00:27.800 --> 00:00:32.660
This atmospheric period film follows the Stewart
family, a mom and her two kids, who start

00:00:32.660 --> 00:00:34.280
to notice that their house is haunted.

00:00:34.440 --> 00:00:38.420
There's a couple roaming the hallways, a ghost
boy hiding behind the curtains, and even a

00:00:38.420 --> 00:00:40.720
freaky blind lady lurking in the shadows.

00:00:40.860 --> 00:00:45.280
But when Grace and her children stumble upon
a séance in the attic, they suddenly realize

00:00:45.280 --> 00:00:46.770
they're the ones who are deceased.

00:00:46.770 --> 00:00:50.340
Her daughter had been right the whole time
about her mother's maniacal ways.

00:00:51.000 --> 00:00:52.200
"She won't stop!

00:00:52.200 --> 00:00:53.120
She won't stop until she

00:00:53.120 --> 00:00:53.940
hurts us."

00:00:54.520 --> 00:00:58.400
As Grace remembers that she did away with
her children and then herself after temporarily

00:00:58.400 --> 00:01:03.300
going insane, she realizes she's damned her
whole family to an eternity inside their creaky

00:01:03.300 --> 00:01:03.860
mansion.

00:01:03.980 --> 00:01:08.900
It's a gut-punch of a twist and also changes
the entire film when you realize the so-called

00:01:08.900 --> 00:01:13.040
ghosts that have been scaring the Stewarts
are actually living people who've moved into

00:01:13.040 --> 00:01:14.020
Grace's old home.

00:01:14.240 --> 00:01:15.880
And they're the ones being haunted.

00:01:16.720 --> 00:01:17.340
Saw

00:01:17.720 --> 00:01:21.960
These days, Jigsaw is one of the most famous
bad guys to ever torture someone on the big

00:01:21.960 --> 00:01:27.180
screen, but in 2004, when the first Saw film
hit theaters, audiences had no idea what the

00:01:27.180 --> 00:01:29.360
infamous serial killer actually looked like.

00:01:29.640 --> 00:01:34.480
In fact, for most of the movie, everybody
suspected that Zep was the psycho who abducted

00:01:34.480 --> 00:01:36.960
and chained up poor Adam in that bathroom
dungeon.

00:01:37.080 --> 00:01:41.800
But after our hero bashes Zep to bits, he
discovers a cassette that reveals the hospital

00:01:41.800 --> 00:01:44.520
orderly was just another victim in Jigsaw's
game.

00:01:44.720 --> 00:01:49.220
And as Adam begins to process this new bit
of info, we watch in horror as a body—which

00:01:49.220 --> 00:01:53.260
has been lying on the bathroom floor for the
whole movie—crawls up off the floor.

00:01:53.380 --> 00:01:58.310
Yep, this corpse is the killer himself, John
Kramer, and when Jigsaw walks out of the bathroom,

00:01:58.310 --> 00:02:02.740
he leaves his latest victim chained to a pipe,
parting with his trademark line:

00:02:03.060 --> 00:02:04.220
"Game over"

00:02:06.000 --> 00:02:10.360
With a doozy like that, it's no wonder the
movie has spawned seven sequels and counting.

00:02:10.940 --> 00:02:11.600
The Mist

00:02:11.980 --> 00:02:15.680
The ending of The Mist is so notorious now
that it really needs no introduction.

00:02:15.780 --> 00:02:18.240
But it's still pretty brilliant and terrible
all the same.

00:02:18.420 --> 00:02:22.780
Director Frank Darabont took a major liberty
with the Stephen King novella to end it the

00:02:22.780 --> 00:02:26.070
way he did, but even King had to compliment
the decision, saying,

00:02:26.070 --> 00:02:27.070
"I loved [it].

00:02:27.070 --> 00:02:28.760
It is the most shocking ending ever."

00:02:28.980 --> 00:02:33.420
The story surrounds a supermarket full of
people who've been trapped inside by an otherworldly

00:02:33.420 --> 00:02:34.820
mist full of monsters.

00:02:35.000 --> 00:02:37.200
But they're not exactly safe from harm there
either.

00:02:37.200 --> 00:02:41.700
As the threat outside continues to dwarf any
escape options, religious zealotry begins

00:02:41.700 --> 00:02:46.100
to overtake some of the survivors, who threaten
to sacrifice our hero David's son.

00:02:46.340 --> 00:02:50.880
So he and the others who reject the apocalyptic
overtures make a break for it after an intense

00:02:50.880 --> 00:02:52.380
stand-off in the checkout aisle.

00:02:52.380 --> 00:02:56.840
Unfortunately, they don't get far before they
run out of gas, and, faced with certain death

00:02:56.840 --> 00:03:01.660
by tentacled terrors, David executes his own
and son and friends with a pistol, but runs

00:03:01.660 --> 00:03:03.940
out of bullets before he can off himself,
too.

00:03:04.080 --> 00:03:08.340
Overcome with instant grief, he goes into
the mist to accept his fate but finds that

00:03:08.340 --> 00:03:11.069
the military has arrived to eradicate the
beasts.

00:03:11.069 --> 00:03:15.180
If only David had waited just a few seconds,
his son would've been okay, and we all could've

00:03:15.360 --> 00:03:17.580
been spared that emotional devastation.

00:03:18.200 --> 00:03:19.360
The Cabin in the Woods

00:03:19.620 --> 00:03:23.780
Possibly the most meta horror movie ever made,
The Cabin in the Woods follows a bunch of

00:03:23.780 --> 00:03:27.580
college students who foolishly spend a weekend
in a creepy forest.

00:03:27.780 --> 00:03:31.420
Naturally, their little getaway doesn't go
as planned, and they quickly discover they're

00:03:31.420 --> 00:03:36.060
meant to be sacrifices in an elaborate ritual
to please some angry ancient entities.

00:03:36.060 --> 00:03:40.700
With a family of undead rednecks hot on their
trail, the two remaining survivors find themselves

00:03:40.820 --> 00:03:44.820
trapped in an underground bunker, surrounded
by a bunch of goons with machine guns.

00:03:44.920 --> 00:03:49.500
Without any other choice, our heroes unleash
an army of monsters, resulting in one of the

00:03:49.500 --> 00:03:52.940
wildest, you-won't-believe-it-until-you-see-it
sequences in horror cinema.

00:03:53.140 --> 00:03:56.820
Pretty much every creature you can imagine
shows up, ready to do some damage.

00:03:57.020 --> 00:04:01.760
We've got a knock off Pennywise, an imitation
Pinhead, and masked murderers straight out

00:04:01.760 --> 00:04:02.680
of The Strangers.

00:04:02.680 --> 00:04:06.260
There's a merman, an enormous bat, and one
unfriendly unicorn.

00:04:06.540 --> 00:04:11.020
By the time the zombies, ghosts, and werewolves
are finished slaughtering everyone in sight,

00:04:11.029 --> 00:04:15.440
the walls are caked with blood, the earth
is doomed, and audiences have had a gory good

00:04:15.440 --> 00:04:15.940
time.

00:04:16.560 --> 00:04:17.360
It Follows

00:04:17.960 --> 00:04:22.599
It's hard to come up with a completely original
movie monster nowadays, but It Follows combined

00:04:22.600 --> 00:04:27.800
the common societal fear of communicable diseases
with traditional terror tropes to create something

00:04:27.800 --> 00:04:28.680
entirely new.

00:04:28.800 --> 00:04:34.140
Basically an STD on two legs, the titular
"It" is spread via contact, and if you contract

00:04:34.220 --> 00:04:37.640
the curse, this enigmatic monster will mercilessly
hunt you down.

00:04:37.780 --> 00:04:42.040
And if it gets you, it then goes after the
person who gave you the curse…and so on

00:04:42.040 --> 00:04:42.880
and so on forever.

00:04:43.040 --> 00:04:47.220
Sure, the creature moves pretty slowly, but
this thing can take any form necessary to

00:04:47.220 --> 00:04:48.740
get close enough to end your life.

00:04:48.900 --> 00:04:51.020
And no matter what, it never stops following.

00:04:51.260 --> 00:04:55.440
Our heroine Jay does her best to fry the monster
with every electronic device she can get her

00:04:55.440 --> 00:04:56.080
hands on.

00:04:56.200 --> 00:05:00.300
And just to play it safe, she gets down with
her friend Paul, who then passes the curse

00:05:00.320 --> 00:05:02.980
on to a prostitute, just in case the thing
comes back.

00:05:03.080 --> 00:05:06.840
And that leads us to the final eerie image
of Jay and Paul walking down a neighborhood

00:05:06.840 --> 00:05:08.920
street, with a man behind them in the distance.

00:05:09.080 --> 00:05:13.500
Maybe it's just a guy walking or maybe it's
the creature that can never die, coming back

00:05:13.509 --> 00:05:14.509
for round two.

00:05:14.509 --> 00:05:18.409
Open endings are often too frustrating to
withstand, but this one fits the theme of

00:05:18.409 --> 00:05:20.660
the film like a glove, if you catch our drift.

00:05:21.480 --> 00:05:22.140
Get Out

00:05:22.140 --> 00:05:26.440
A modern-day masterpiece, Jordan Peele's Get
Out almost had a radically different ending.

00:05:26.440 --> 00:05:30.800
Originally, Peele planned on having his main
character, Chris Washington, arrested after

00:05:30.800 --> 00:05:33.600
escaping the clutches of the mind-controlling
family.

00:05:33.800 --> 00:05:37.920
Fortunately, the writer-director had a change
of heart and crafted a new ending that left

00:05:37.930 --> 00:05:40.529
audiences cheering instead of crying.

00:05:40.529 --> 00:05:45.069
To set the scene, Chris has just narrowly
avoided the lobotomy to end all lobotomies,

00:05:45.069 --> 00:05:49.279
and during his getaway, he dispatches every
evil white person who steps into his path.

00:05:49.280 --> 00:05:53.409
This eventually ends with Chris standing above
his psycho ex-girlfriend as she's bleeding

00:05:53.409 --> 00:05:54.480
out on a country road.

00:05:54.620 --> 00:05:59.120
Suddenly, flashing lights appear in the distance,
and we assume the worst is about to happen.

00:05:59.480 --> 00:06:02.260
"No""No""No""No""No""No""No""No""No""No""No""No"

00:06:02.780 --> 00:06:06.460
But instead of the law showing up to cart
Chris away, who should step out of the car

00:06:06.470 --> 00:06:09.570
but Chris's best friend, TSA Officer Rod Williams.

00:06:09.570 --> 00:06:13.900
As Rod takes Chris back to safety, everyone
in the audience breathes a sigh of relief,

00:06:14.020 --> 00:06:17.660
knowing full-well this kind of upbeat ending
rarely happens in real life.

00:06:17.980 --> 00:06:18.940
Thanks for watching!

00:06:19.180 --> 00:06:21.860
